[{"id":13744,"sender_id":14,"sender_full_name":"TobyBartels","avatar_url":"https://secure.gravatar.com/avatar/7ac66e2e51d2a389b2ab9b2a99100a0c?d=identicon&version=1","content":"<p><a href=\"#narrow/channel/17-n-Forum/topic/Error.20report.3A.20.60.5Ccdot.60.20doesn.27t.20work.20in.20iTeX.2E/near/13744\">#1</a> <a href=\"http://www.math.ntnu.no/~stacey/Vanilla/nForum/comments.php?DiscussionID=1550&amp;Focus=13766#Comment_13766\">Todd noticed</a> that <code>\\cdot</code> doesn’t work in iTeX.</p>\n<p>Examples: <span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-mathml\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mo>⋅</mo></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">\\cdot</annotation></semantics></math></span><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"base\"><span class=\"strut\" style=\"height:0.4445em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\">⋅</span></span></span></span>, <span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-mathml\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>⋅</mo><mi>b</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">a \\cdot b</annotation></semantics></math></span><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"base\"><span class=\"strut\" style=\"height:0.4445em;\"></span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\">a</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2222em;\"></span><span class=\"mbin\">⋅</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2222em;\"></span></span><span class=\"base\"><span class=\"strut\" style=\"height:0.6944em;\"></span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\">b</span></span></span></span>.</p>","timestamp":1279044888,"subject":"Error report: `\\cdot` doesn't work in iTeX.","stream_id":17,"display_recipient":"n-Forum","reactions":[]},{"id":13880,"sender_id":9,"sender_full_name":"Andrew Stacey","avatar_url":"https://secure.gravatar.com/avatar/59e0a28758c4f6630d67fe7138b37311?d=identicon&version=1","content":"<p><a href=\"#narrow/channel/17-n-Forum/topic/Error.20report.3A.20.60.5Ccdot.60.20doesn.27t.20work.20in.20iTeX.2E/near/13880\">#2</a> This is a bug in the iTeX on the nForum only and not on the nLab.  I need to update the itex cgi binary on mathforge to fix this (it’s a typo in the entity produced by the <code>\\cdot</code> command).  Shall do so at the next opportunity.</p>","timestamp":1279310278,"subject":"Error report: `\\cdot` doesn't work in iTeX.","stream_id":17,"display_recipient":"n-Forum","reactions":[]},{"id":13914,"sender_id":9,"sender_full_name":"Andrew Stacey","avatar_url":"https://secure.gravatar.com/avatar/59e0a28758c4f6630d67fe7138b37311?d=identicon&version=1","content":"<p><a href=\"#narrow/channel/17-n-Forum/topic/Error.20report.3A.20.60.5Ccdot.60.20doesn.27t.20work.20in.20iTeX.2E/near/13914\">#3</a> Fixed!  And retrospectively, as evidenced by the fact that Toby’s bug report no longer demonstrates the bug.</p>","timestamp":1279487071,"subject":"Error report: `\\cdot` doesn't work in iTeX.","stream_id":17,"display_recipient":"n-Forum","reactions":[]}]